 * an advisory lock alone would not survive a second process on a second host.
 *
 * `status` and `failed_at` record the outcome so a failed spawn is visibly failed rather than
 * silently un-run — a firing row is claimed BEFORE the driver is called and resolved after, so a
 * crash mid-spawn leaves evidence instead of a gap.
